        "title": "[codex] chore: refresh Actions runtimes and toolchain",
        "body": "## What changed\n\n- refresh the GitHub Actions runtime stack: cache v6, Pages v5, GitHub App token v3.2.0, and pnpm action v6.0.9\n- move the repository toolchain to pnpm 11.10.0, Bun 1.3.14, Wrangler 4.107.0, and current compatible formatting/lint packages\n- keep Node types on the Node 24 line and update the native TypeScript preview only to the newest build past the release-age gate\n- add regression coverage for exact action pins and cache-generation alignment\n\n## Why\n\nThe repository is already standardized on Node 24 and checkout v7. This keeps the remaining Actions and package tooling on their current supported runtimes while preserving the existing workflow behavior and exact supply-chain pins.\n\n## Impact\n\nNo ClawSweeper product behavior or worker-capacity policy changes. CI, Pages, dashboard deployment, and local development use supported current toolchains.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `pnpm run check` (694 unit tests, 622 repair tests, coverage, formatting)\n- focused Actions/workflow tests: 154 passed\n- `pnpm audit`: zero vulnerabilities\n- local Codex preflight with `gpt-5.5`\n- Wrangler 4.107.0 dashboard deployment dry-run\n- fresh AutoReview: no findings\n\nHosted Actions, CodeQL, Pages, and dashboard checks on this exact head remain the merge gates.\n",
